   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "2\u20133 real options; the current proposal is only one of them",
   "originalText": "2\u20133 real options; the current proposal is only one of them",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "adr-optA",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 40,
   "y": 489.0,
   "width": 480,
   "height": 374,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#868e96",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 185707817,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 348216466,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "id": "adr-optA-text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "adr-optA-text",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 46,
   "y": 495.0,
   "width": 468,
   "height": 300.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 198951483,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1987151421,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "A. Keep requirements in code\n\nHow it works: questions, search words and rules stay\nin evidence.py; a new standard is new code.\n\nPros:\n\u2022 no change now\n\u2022 rules are plain Python\n\nCons:\n\u2022 the check is tied to one standard\n\u2022 changing \"what counts\" needs a programmer\n\u2022 the prompt keeps naming the source\n\nMark (current state)",
   "originalText": "A. Keep requirements in code\n\nHow it works: questions, search words and rules stay\nin evidence.py; a new standard is new code.\n\nPros:\n\u2022 no change now\n\u2022 rules are plain Python\n\nCons:\n\u2022 the check is tied to one standard\n\u2022 changing \"what counts\" needs a programmer\n\u2022 the prompt keeps naming the source\n\nMark (current state)",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "adr-optA",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "adr-optB",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 550,
   "y": 489.0,
   "width": 480,
   "height": 374,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
   "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1204451460,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 2023960738,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "id": "adr-optB-text"
    }
   ],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "adr-optB-text",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 556,
   "y": 495.0,
   "width": 468,
   "height": 360.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1472500626,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 623039801,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "B. Requirement sets as data files\n\nHow it works: checks/requirements/<name>.json lists\nwhat must be reported (questions, search hints,\nwhich documents to read) and how \"enough\" is\ndecided, using a small vocabulary of rule types the\ncode provides; the prompt is generic and the facts\ncome from data.\n\nPros:\n\u2022 one generic check for any standard\n\u2022 readable, reviewable in git like prompts\n\u2022 logged per run with its fingerprint\n\nCons:\n\u2022 the rule vocabulary must cover each standard\n\nMark (proposal)",
   "originalText": "B. Requirement sets as data files\n\nHow it works: checks/requirements/<name>.json lists\nwhat must be reported (questions, search hints,\nwhich documents to read) and how \"enough\" is\ndecided, using a small vocabulary of rule types the\ncode provides; the prompt is generic and the facts\ncome from data.\n\nPros:\n\u2022 one generic check for any standard\n\u2022 readable, reviewable in git like prompts\n\u2022 logged per run with its fingerprint\n\nCons:\n\u2022 the rule vocabulary must cover each standard\n\nMark (proposal)",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "adr-optB",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
